  "key_evidence": [
    "CMU expanded Title VI/IEX investigations of Fence painters from 8 to 10 individuals and interim campus-access restrictions from 7 to 9 between 13 and 29 July 2026, with one student facing possible expulsion (The Tartan, 13 and 29 July 2026).",
    "CMU's stated basis is that the messages constituted 'discriminatory harassment on the basis of race, national origin, and/or religion, related to statements made on the Fence and/or posted to social media' — sanction applied to speech on the university's own designated free-expression structure (The Tartan, 29 July 2026).",
    "Some sanctioned messages were painted by Jewish students criticising Zionism; nine organisations including Jewish Voice for Peace and Palestine Legal issued a joint condemnation on 28 July 2026.",
    "On 28 July 2026 CMU revised its discrimination policy and code of business ethics following a 'C' rating from an external advocacy organisation and described a prohibition on anti-Israel conduct in the revised text as a typographical error (The Tartan, 28 July 2026).",
    "An Academic Workers United petition calling on the university to 'maintain the liberty/legacy of free expression on [the] Fence' had passed 400 signatures by 29 July 2026."
  ],
